  "note": "Patterns are regular expressions matched against the whole object name. An object is excluded first, then mapped to the first id that matches (no object may match two ids), then put in the head group when it lies in a head collection (never drawn, the face is the CC0 head or the smooth shell, but still part of the body the skin is built from), then hidden when it matches a hidden pattern, then drawn neutral when it matches the neutral rules, and is otherwise deep and not drawn. A trim removes the faces of one id that lie within a distance of another id's surface, which is how the external oblique aponeurosis is cut away from the rectus abdominis. Z-Anatomy names the trapezius parts the wrong way round: its Ascending part is the upper fibres at the neck and its Descending part is the lower fibres between the shoulder blades, so traps_upper takes the Ascending part and traps_mid takes the Descending part.",
